---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { getSiteData } from '../lib/baserow';

const data=await getSiteData();
const s=data.settings;
const contactEmail=s.contactEmail||'info@rootedcommons.uk';
---
<BaseLayout settings={s} pages={data.pages} title="Membership terms" description="The terms that apply to Rooted Commons membership, Member Credit and your regular commitment.">
  <main class="legal-page">
    <article class="legal-content">
      <p class="eyebrow">Rooted Commons</p>
      <h1>Membership terms</h1>
      <p class="small-print">Last updated: 15 August 2026</p>

      <p>These terms explain the ongoing Rooted Commons membership relationship. By joining, you agree to these terms. Individual purchases are also subject to our <a href="/terms-of-sale/">Terms of Sale</a>. Nothing in these terms reduces your statutory rights.</p>

      <h2>1. About your membership</h2>
      <p>Rooted Commons is a membership-based buying network operated by Roots to Fruits CIC, connecting members with local produce, cupboard staples, refills and other goods supplied through our network. Membership gives you access to the weekly market, your member account and our collection-point network.</p>
      <p><strong>Rooted Commons membership is not membership of Roots to Fruits CIC.</strong> Joining does not make you a statutory member, shareholder or company member of Roots to Fruits CIC and does not give you voting or governance rights in the CIC.</p>
      <p>Please keep your contact details reasonably up to date and keep your weekly access link private. It can be used to sign in on a new device. Tell us promptly if you think somebody else has used it.</p>

      <h2>2. Your regular commitment</h2>
      <p>Membership involves a regular commitment equivalent to at least £10 per week. You can choose to contribute weekly (minimum £10.00) or monthly (minimum £43.33), using a standing order or another payment method we expressly make available. Your chosen frequency and amount are shown in your member account.</p>
      <p>This is a genuine commitment to spending through the Rooted Commons network. You control your standing order through your own bank and can stop future payments if you decide to leave.</p>

      <h2>3. Pauses, streaks and missed regular payments</h2>
      <p>You can arrange a pause of your regular commitment for up to eight weeks in each calendar year. Unused pause weeks do not roll over. During an agreed pause, your consecutive-weeks streak is frozen rather than increased or reset. Member perks you have already unlocked remain available, and you may still place orders. Routine weekly-market emails and regular-payment reminders are normally suppressed during the pause.</p>
      <p>Your consecutive-weeks streak records sustained regular support rather than whether you place an order every week. A matching weekly regular payment adds one supporting week and a matching monthly regular payment adds four supporting weeks.</p>
      <p>If an expected regular payment does not arrive and no pause has been arranged, your streak is frozen for a grace period of one calendar month from the missed-payment date. If the payment resumes within that period, the streak continues from the frozen total; missed weeks are not added. If the issue remains unresolved after one calendar month, the membership becomes inactive, the streak ends and progression-based perks reset. We retain the previous streak figure so that exceptional circumstances can be reviewed where appropriate.</p>

      <h2>4. Member Credit</h2>
      <p>Payments received are added to your Member Credit. Unspent credit rolls over for future Rooted Commons orders. Member Credit is not a bank or savings account.</p>
      <p>You need sufficient Member Credit to pay for an order before it is fulfilled. If your balance is insufficient, we may reserve the order while you top up and may cancel it if sufficient payment is not received by the relevant deadline.</p>

      <h2>5. Ordering and collection</h2>
      <p>Active members can order through the weekly market using Member Credit. We normally issue a new weekly access link each Wednesday after orders close. A new weekly link replaces the previous link for new sign-ins, but a device that is already signed in can remain signed in for up to 90 days unless you sign out or clear your browser data. Current opening and closing times shown on the website apply.</p>
      <p>All orders are delivered to collection points on Thursday. Some locations support late collection of fresh produce on Friday, but only suitable items, such as cupboard staples and refills, can be held for collection over the weekend. Collection preferences can be changed at checkout or through your dashboard, subject to availability.</p>
      <p>Our <a href="/terms-of-sale/">Terms of Sale</a> explain the rules applying to individual purchases, including availability, cancellations and returns, product information, collection and your rights if there is a problem with something you buy.</p>

      <h2>6. Inactive and closed memberships</h2>
      <p>You can end your membership by contacting us and stopping future standing-order payments. If no regular payment is received for one calendar month and no pause has been arranged, your membership becomes inactive. We stop routine weekly-market emails at that point. You can restart an inactive membership by resuming your regular commitment, although a new consecutive-weeks streak starts unless we agree to reinstate the previous streak because of exceptional circumstances.</p>
      <p>If no regular payment is received for six calendar months from the first missed expected payment, we normally close the inactive membership and revoke active sign-in sessions. Closing the membership does not forfeit unused Member Credit. If you still have Member Credit, contact us and we will agree how the remaining balance should be returned or used. This may include spending it through the market, a partner voucher where you agree to this, or a refund where appropriate. Nothing in these terms limits any refund or other remedy you are entitled to by law.</p>

      <h2>7. Communications and changes</h2>
      <p>We use your email address to send the secure links and service messages needed to operate your membership. We may use your phone number where reasonably necessary to resolve a time-sensitive issue. Optional Rooted Commons news is based on your separate choice and can be switched off without affecting your membership.</p>
      <p>We may make reasonable changes to how Rooted Commons operates as the service develops, including collection arrangements and the ordering process. If we make a significant change to these terms, the minimum commitment or how Member Credit works, we will tell you before the change takes effect. If you do not wish to continue under a significant change, you can end your membership.</p>

      <h2>8. Contact and legal rights</h2>
      <p>Questions about membership or these terms can be sent to <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>.</p>
      <p>Nothing in these terms limits your statutory rights or any liability that cannot legally be limited.</p>
      <p>These terms are governed by the law of England and Wales. If you live elsewhere in the United Kingdom, you may also have mandatory rights under the law that applies where you live.</p>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
